   "title": "Note: Guide",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Breeze Voice Design\n\nDescribe a voice in words and get a usable voice back, plus a spoken preview of it. No sample audio needed.\n\n### How to use\n\n1. Sign in with your ComfyUI account. This is an API node, so it bills per use.\n2. Write the **description**: 3 to 500 characters covering age, gender, accent, tone and pace. Concrete beats poetic - \"warm male, mid-forties, soft Scottish accent, close-miked, unhurried\" lands better than \"a nice voice\".\n3. Write the **preview_text**: up to 500 characters, in the selected **language**. This line is what the model builds the voice from, so write it in the register you want the voice to speak in.\n4. `strength` (1 to 10) says how literally the model follows the description. Raise it when the result drifts, lower it when the voice sounds strained.\n5. Queue the prompt. The node returns two outputs: `voice` (plug it into Text to Speech, Remix or Localize) and `preview` (the audio you hear and save here).\n6. Pick a seed you like and keep `control_after_generate` on `fixed` to reproduce it; switch to `randomize` to audition variations.\n"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## Breeze Voice Design\n\nDescribe a voice in words and get a usable voice back, plus a spoken preview of it. No sample audio needed.\n\n### How to use\n\n1. Sign in with your ComfyUI account. This is an API node, so it bills per use.\n2. Write the **description**: 3 to 500 characters covering age, gender, accent, tone and pace. Concrete beats poetic - \"warm male, mid-forties, soft Scottish accent, close-miked, unhurried\" lands better than \"a nice voice\".\n3. Write the **preview_text**: up to 500 characters, in the selected **language**. This line is what the model builds the voice from, so write it in the register you want the voice to speak in.\n4. `strength` (1 to 10) says how literally the model follows the description. Raise it when the result drifts, lower it when the voice sounds strained.\n5. Queue the prompt. The node returns two outputs: `voice` (plug it into Text to Speech, Remix or Localize) and `preview` (the audio you hear and save here).\n6. Pick a seed you like and keep `control_after_generate` on `fixed` to reproduce it; switch to `randomize` to audition variations.\n"
   }
  }
